# What must NOT reach the image. Dockerfile:25 is `COPY . .`, so this file is the only thing
# standing between the build context and the layer. /audit demonstrated on 2026-09-02 that
# without it a `.env` present in the context is baked in, SECRET_KEY and all.
#
# Keep in mind what the container genuinely needs at runtime:
#   app/          the application
#   alembic/      + alembic.ini — the CMD runs `alembic upgrade head` on every start
#   scripts/      registration_code.py is run with `docker compose exec backend python ...`
#   requirements.txt
# Everything else is build-host clutter, and some of it is a credential.

# --- secrets. The reason this file exists. ---
.env
.env.*

# --- version control history (3.2 MB, and it does not belong in a runtime image) ---
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
.github
.gitleaks.toml

# --- the build host's virtualenv: wrong platform, and it shadows the image's own packages ---
venv
.venv

# --- test, coverage and lint artefacts ---
tests
pytest.ini
.pytest_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
.ruff_cache
.import_linter_cache
.harness-baseline
test_bulk_logging.sh

# --- caches and editor droppings ---
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.DS_Store

# --- docs and process files ---
docs
specs
*.md
justfile
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
